course: dictionary
lesson: 5639
title: Stay a little longer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To linger is to stay somewhere longer than you need to, because you do not want to leave or you are in no hurry. «I will linger, and look back» tells you the speaker is slow to go. They keep stopping and turning round.
explain: Linger can also describe things that stay for a long time. A smell of toast can linger in the kitchen, and a cold can linger for weeks. The word tells you that something is slow to go away.
explain: To linger over something means to take your time with it. «Well, well, we won't linger over that now» means we will not spend a long time on it at the moment. Context clues like «look back», «corridors» and «gate» help you work out the meaning.
fact: Linger is a verb: linger, lingers, lingered, lingering.
fact: «Linger» means to stay somewhere longer than usual or than needed.
fact: «Linger» can describe a smell, a feeling or an illness that stays for a long time.
fact: «Linger over» something means to take your time with it, or not spend long on it.
fact: A good check is to swap in the word stay and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «She lingered at the gate.» What does lingered mean here? | *Stayed longer, not wanting to leave | Ran off quickly | Climbed over the wall | Shut the gate loudly
exercise: A cold can linger for weeks. What does linger mean here? | Turns into snow | Makes a loud noise | Goes away at once | *Stays for a long time
exercise: «Don't linger in the corridors.» What is the teacher asking you to do? | *Keep moving and do not stay around | Sing as you walk | Sit down and rest in the corridor | Stay as long as you like
test: Which word is closest in meaning to linger? | Forget | Jump | *Stay | Shout
test: «We won't linger over that now.» What does this mean? | We will spend hours on it now | We will pass it to someone else | *We will not spend time on it now | We will forget it forever
exam: Which sentence uses linger correctly? | The cat lingers the milk into the sink | I lingered my homework in the bin | *After the storm, the smell of rain will linger in the garden | Please linger your bag to school
